Replacing $x$ by $x - a$ gives $y = f(x - a)$, which shifts the graph right by $a$ units when $a > 0$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
\draw[->] (-2.6,0) -- (3.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.0) -- (0,2.0) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, gray, <->, domain=-2.2:1.6, samples=80, smooth, variable=\x] plot ({\x}, {0.4*\x*\x*\x + 0.5*\x*\x - 1.2*\x - 0.6});
\draw[thick, blue, <->, domain=-1.0:2.8, samples=80, smooth, variable=\x] plot ({\x}, {0.4*(\x-1.2)*(\x-1.2)*(\x-1.2) + 0.5*(\x-1.2)*(\x-1.2) - 1.2*(\x-1.2) - 0.6});
\draw[->, red, thick] (0.667,-1.059) -- (1.867,-1.059);
\node[red] at (1.267,-1.62) {right $a$};
\node[gray] at (-1.6,1.55) {$y=f(x)$};
\node[blue] at (1.9,1.55) {$y=f(x-a)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Replacing $y$ by $y - b$ instead gives $y = f(x) + b$, which shifts the graph up by $b$ units when $b > 0$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
\draw[->] (-2.8,0) -- (3.0,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.0) -- (0,3.1) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, gray, <->, domain=-2.2:1.6, samples=80, smooth, variable=\x] plot ({\x}, {0.4*\x*\x*\x + 0.5*\x*\x - 1.2*\x - 0.6});
\draw[thick, blue, <->, domain=-2.2:1.6, samples=80, smooth, variable=\x] plot ({\x}, {0.4*\x*\x*\x + 0.5*\x*\x - 1.2*\x + 0.6});
\draw[->, red, thick] (1.5,0.075) -- (1.5,1.275);
\node[red] at (2.35,0.675) {up $b$};
\node[gray] at (-1.3,-1.55) {$y=f(x)$};
\node[blue] at (-1.3,2.65) {$y=f(x)+b$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
Find the equation of the circle $x^2 + y^2 = 16$ after it is translated $2$ units right and $3$ units up.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.6]
\draw[->] (-5.2,0) -- (5.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-5.2) -- (0,5.2) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {-4,4} {
  \draw (\x,0.15) -- (\x,-0.15);
}
\foreach \y in {-4,4} {
  \draw (0.15,\y) -- (-0.15,\y);
}
\node[below right] at (4,0) {$4$};
\node[below left] at (-4,0) {$-4$};
\node[above left] at (0,4) {$4$};
\node[below left] at (0,-4) {$-4$};
\draw[thick] (0,0) circle (4);
\fill (0,0) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below left] at (0,0) {$O$};
\node[above right] at (2.83,2.83) {$x^2 + y^2 = 16$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

