The hyperbola $y = \dfrac{1}{x} + 4$ has asymptotes $x = 0$ and $y = 4$.
State the equations of the asymptotes after a translation of $3$ units right and $2$ units down.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.6]
\draw[->] (-4.5,0) -- (4.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.2) -- (0,9.2) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {-4,-2,2,4} {
  \draw (\x,0.15) -- (\x,-0.15) node[below, font=\scriptsize] {$\x$};
}
\foreach \y in {-1,2,4,6,8} {
  \draw (0.15,\y) -- (-0.15,\y) node[left, font=\scriptsize] {$\y$};
}
\node[below left, font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[dashed, thick] (-4.5,4) -- (4.5,4) node[right] {$y=4$};
\draw[dashed, thick] (0,-2.2) -- (0,8.8) node[above right] {$x=0$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=0.23:4.2, samples=60, smooth, variable=\x] plot ({\x}, {1/\x + 4});
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-4.2:-0.18, samples=60, smooth, variable=\x] plot ({\x}, {1/\x + 4});
\node[above right] at (1.5,5.5) {$y = \dfrac{1}{x} + 4$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
